 red granite cliffs 07", "source": "mediawiki-metadata"}, "CommonsMetadataExtension": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "CC-Zero|Stångehuvud|Bohus Granite|Self-published work|Images by W.carter|Images from Wiki Loves Earth 2017|Sweden photographs taken on 2017-06-13|Images from Wiki Loves Earth 2017 in Sweden|Protected areas of Sweden with known IDs|Content made available through Wikimedia Sverige competitions|Uploaded via Campaign:wle-se|Images from Wiki Loves Earth missing SDC depicts|Granite formations at Stångehuvud|Islands in Lysekil", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "GPSLatitude": {"value": "58.269005", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "GPSLongitude": {"value": "11.417357", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "GPSMapDatum": {"value": "WGS-84", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "The glittering cliffs at <a href=\"https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/St%C3%A5ngehuvuds_naturreservat\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"sv:Stångehuvuds naturreservat\">Stångehuvud nature reserve</a> in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lysekil\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Lysekil\">Lysekil</a>, Sweden. The red <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granite\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Granite\">granite</a> cliffs are noted for their colour and the large <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feldspar\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Feldspar\">feldspar</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/mica\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:mica\">mica</a> crystals (about 10 x 10 mm) that make any part of the cliffs glitter when the sun reflects off them. The cliffs in the nature reserve were saved from quarrying at the beginning of the 20th century by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calla_Curman\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Calla Curman\">Calla Curman</a>. She bought the whole area and donated it to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Swedish_Academy_of_Sciences\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences\">Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences</a> in 1925.<br>This image illustrates how light, at different angles, is reflected off the feldspar crystals in the rock.<br><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Lysekil_granite.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Red_Lysekil_granite.jpg/120px-Red_Lysekil_granite.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"128\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Red_Lysekil_granite.jpg/250px-Red_Lysekil_granite.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3161\" data-file-height=\"3364\"></a></span>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "2017-06-13 16:09:27", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:W.carter\" title=\"User:W.carter\">W.carter</a>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "CC0", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "UsageTerms": {"value": "Creative Commons Zero, Public Domain Dedication", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "AttributionRequired": {"value": "false", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "LicenseUrl": {"value": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Copyrighted": {"value": "True", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Restrictions": {"value": "", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "License": {"value": "cc0", "source": "commons-templates", "hidden": ""}}}]}]}}